prompt:
Take the reference photograph of the hospital room and move the camera only: a new real photograph of the SAME room, the same morning and the same light, taken from closer, standing beside the bedside cabinet on the left of the reference photograph and looking down at its top from a little above, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Every object keeps exactly its shape, its colour and its place from the reference photograph; only the camera has come closer.

The top of the small white bedside cabinet fills the lower half of the picture, seen from above at a slant, with the plain white cabinet front and its one drawer below it. On the cabinet top and on its open shelf, each thing apart from the others, with a band of plain white cabinet top around it:
- the clear drinking glass half full of water;
- the plastic feeding cup with its pale-blue spouted lid and two side handles;
- the pair of reading glasses lying folded;
- the small skin-coloured hearing aid lying on the folded white paper tissue at the left end of the cabinet top;
- and below the drawer, on the open shelf of the cabinet, the small closed white-and-pale-blue plastic denture box, exactly as in the reference photograph.

Behind the cabinet, in the upper half of the picture: at the right, the white duvet of the bed with the old man's hand lying on it, the plain white plastic band around his wrist; at the left, the folded pale-green privacy screen; and between them the slim steel pole of the drip stand.

The whole picture carries no writing, numbers, print, symbol or logo anywhere, exactly as in the reference photograph.
